course: dictionary
lesson: 7733
title: Many meanings of pull
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «Lily stays with Chloe in the nurse's room after Chloe's plaits are pulled so hard she cries.» Here pull means tug hard on something, and the crying tells you it hurt.
explain: «A horse walking on the tow-path pulls a barge with a long rope.» Pull means to move something toward you, or along behind you, by holding it. Try swapping in drags. It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Pull has other meanings too. «Pull out» or «pull up» means take something out, as in pull weeds. A pull can also be a force: gravity is a pull that draws things down. Look at the words around pull to decide which meaning fits.
fact: To pull is to move something toward you by holding it.
fact: To pull out or pull up means to take something out, such as pulling weeds or a tooth.
fact: A pull is a force that draws things closer, like the pull of a magnet or of gravity.
fact: With several pulleys, you pull with less force but must pull much more rope.
fact: A vehicle pulls in, out or over when it moves to the side or stops.
exercise: «A horse walking on the tow-path pulls a barge with a long rope.» What does pulls mean here? | Paints it bright blue | Pushes it away | Sleeps on it | *Moves it toward itself by holding it
exercise: Science says gravity pulls things down. What is a pull in this sentence? | A colour | A kind of food | *A force that draws things closer | A sound
exercise: «Lily stays with Chloe in the nurse's room after Chloe's plaits are pulled so hard she cries.» Find and copy one word that means pulled hard on. | cries | *pulled | nurse | room
test: «A vehicle pulls over when it moves to the side or stops.» What does pulls over mean? | *It moves to the side of the road and stops | It flies up into the air | It turns into a boat | It goes much faster
test: Why does an adult or doctor remove a fish hook stuck in a finger, instead of pulling it out? | Because a magnet holds it | *Because the barb tears skin | Because the hook is too heavy | Because fingers are too small to hold it
exam: In «pull weeds», what does pull mean? | Sing loudly | *Take out of the ground | Read quietly | Paint
